  "notes": "Exact distance: d_X = d_Z = 13. Two independently written exhaustive searches (exactA, exactB), anchored at the translations of Z_31, find no nontrivial logical of weight <= 12 on either side (records and the certificate certs/434-62-13.json); dist-m4ri 0.16.1 and tropidist b03ec2d4077f, run without symmetry, give the same value on both sides. Definitions, records and a rebuild script: github.com/TimoKellerMath/quantum-error-correction @ 2a15e549f6f4, pair-partition-and-two-block-codes/434-62-13/ and pair-partition-and-two-block-codes/src/rebuild.py. Novelty claim: new parameters only. No entry of board commit 82a52ee51 has n = 434 and k = 62, no published code with these parameters is known to us (literature search of 2026-11-11: see the note), at that commit no CSS entry dominates or equals it in (n, k, d, w), and it dominates 36 entries (see the note). Construction and attribution: a CPM lift of a sparse 6x14 template (check weight 6, column degrees 2 and 3) whose X/Z row overlaps are made even by pair partitions with the girth rule of Okada and Kasai (arXiv:2607.14091); their codes and Kasai's catalogue use all-one JxL templates with check weight L >= 8, as do arXiv:2609.30069 and arXiv:2609.35601. Relation to the board (export 82a52ee51): CPM lifts whose X/Z row overlaps split into pairs of equal exponent difference are common on the board at check weights 4 to 8, among them two-block and bicycle codes, the [[6N,2N+2,6]] family of arXiv:2610.19451 (all-one 2x6 template, d = 6) and irregular templates such as 260-58-6 and the 14x28 lifts 280-20-8 to 700-50-8 at check weight 6; entries tagged pair-partition-cpm occur only at check weight >= 7 (e.g. 990-198-17, 994-142-40, 972-166-34). In the layouts tested (consecutive or interleaved blocks of the stored qubit order), no entry of check weight 6 is a lift of a template with column degrees 2 and 3 (computed). No entry has these n and k; checked, not equivalent to an existing entry."
